{
  "what": "Choosing get_promises' description, 2026-10-16. Nova Pro under the Alexa bridge's prompt ran the whole corpus for each wording, in parallel batches against one local server per wording; Nova runs close together are correlated, so compare within a batch. Claude Sonnet 4.5 (console prompt) ran one full corpus on the kept wording (2026-10-16-claude-sonnet-4-5-get-promises.json); the cases that moved were then run alone, 3 times per wording. A full Sonnet comparison was not possible: these runs hit the account's daily Bedrock token quota. A Sonnet run keeps only its failures, so a passing row has chosen: null.",
  "descriptions": {
    "V1 (dropped): shorter, fewer example questions, points gaps to get_care_gaps": "What people in the family said yes to this week, and what has happened since: who said yes, any \"still on?\" check-in and its answer, whether it was handed back or marked done. For \"what did everyone say yes to?\", \"who promised what?\". Only what was agreed in this family's care; for what still needs doing or has no owner, use get_care_gaps. Read-only. Speak the result as written: work due with nothing marked is \"nothing's been marked yet\", never a promise broken.",
    "V2 (dropped): current plus V1's get_care_gaps sentence": "The kept description with \"what has the family taken on this week?\" shortened to \"...taken on?\" and this added before \"Read-only.\": \"Only what someone agreed to in this family's care; for what still needs doing or has no owner, use get_care_gaps.\""
